Feature: Filter list by tag

  `yx list --tag <name>` filters to yaks with the given tag.
  Non-matching yaks (and their subtrees) are hidden.

  Rule: Single tag filter

    `--tag foo` shows only yaks tagged `foo`, hiding everything else.

    Example: Shows yak with matching tag, hides others

      Given a yak "deploy" tagged "epic"
      And a yak "fix bug" tagged "urgent"
      When I run `yx list --tag epic --format plain`
      Then the output should contain "deploy"
      But the output should not contain "fix bug"

    Example: Hides untagged yaks

      Given a yak "cleanup" with no tags
      When I run `yx list --tag epic --format plain`
      Then the output should not contain "cleanup"

  Rule: Combines with --only

    `--tag` and `--only` are ANDed.

    Example: --tag epic --only done shows only done yaks with epic tag

      Given a yak "A" tagged "epic" with state "done"
      And a yak "B" tagged "epic" with state "todo"
      When I run `yx list --tag epic --only done --format plain`
      Then the output should contain "A"
      But the output should not contain "B"

  Rule: Tag normalization

    The @ prefix is stripped, same as yx tag add.

    Example: --tag @epic treated same as --tag epic

      Given a yak "A" tagged "epic"
      When I run `yx list --tag @epic --format plain`
      Then the output should contain "A"

  Rule: No matches

    Empty result when nothing matches.

    Example: JSON format returns empty array

      Given a yak "A" tagged "urgent"
      When I run `yx list --tag epic --format json`
      Then the output should be "[]"

  Rule: IDs format

    `--format ids` outputs just yak IDs, one per line.
    Useful for piping into other commands.

    Example: Lists yak IDs one per line

      Given a yak "deploy" with id "deploy-a1b2"
      And a yak "cleanup" with id "cleanup-c3d4"
      When I run `yx list --format ids`
      Then the output should be "deploy-a1b2\ncleanup-c3d4"

    Example: Combined with --tag for filtered IDs

      Given a yak "deploy" with id "deploy-a1b2" tagged "epic"
      And a yak "cleanup" with id "cleanup-c3d4"
      When I run `yx list --tag epic --format ids`
      Then the output should be "deploy-a1b2"
